  "review": {
    "review": "The hero died to a skeleton, explicitly identified by the full terminal public message at decision 2771, accepted log line 8012. An earlier actionable defect occurred at decision 2751: after stepping behind door 724 to cell 687, the bot waited for a remembered DM-100 while an awake prison guard stood diagonally adjacent. The accepted wait at line 7933 reduced HP from 27 to 19. The immediate-safety doorway controller checked the remembered caster's sight but omitted other observed attackers before its first wait. The proposed narrow correction yields that bank commitment whenever current observed exposure is nonzero; it does not choose or certify a replacement action. A reduced public-geometry regression failed with the expected assertion on original policy and passed after correction. The full suite passed 2033 tests with four skips. The fixture's plan is reconstructed, not recorded memory; an earlier helper reconstruction diverged at decision 2747 and stopped there. No changed-decision continuation or survival claim is made. Pre-death unknown item identities were not inferred from death revelations.",
    "learnings": "Breaking one caster's sight does not make a waiting square safe from another attacker. Check current contact and ranged exposure before the first lure wait, not only after damage arrives. A conservative veto is not evidence that the downstream action will save the hero."
  },
